            <chunk name="Object" index="2">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">4f2b8c1e-93d7-4a60-b5e2-7c1d0a9e3f64</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">82b21a65-da8f-433c-93fb-f9814609e1d6</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">LiDAR Site</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="7">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fetch open LiDAR and building footprints for a site from its latitude and longitude, for City Surface: the footprints over a square of the given Size, the point cloud (the terrain) over a larger square, Terrain Size — the ground a CFD domain stands on reaches further than the buildings that matter. The Netherlands: AHN (Het Waterschapshuis, CC-BY 4.0) from its official sheets — a sheet is ~5 GB and is downloaded once into the cache, then every site in it is read from there — with BAG footprints (Kadaster, CC0). The United States: USGS 3DEP (public domain), only the point-cloud nodes over the site, with GlobalBuildingAtlas footprints (TUM, CC BY-NC 4.0; OpenStreetMap if it cannot be read). France (IGN LiDAR HD, Licence Ouverte), Switzerland (swissSURFACE3D, swisstopo), Bavaria (CC BY 4.0), Scotland (National LiDAR Programme, OGL) and Estonia (Maa- ja Ruumiamet): the 1 km tiles over the site, 65-155 MB each, cached once, with the same footprints. Everything comes out in metres around the site centre: wire Point Cloud, Footprints and Domain into City Surface. Tree Crowns are read from the cloud's own vegetation returns (one closed mesh per cluster, for the Tree component); Land Cover, Land Cover Names, Roughness and Flatten are OpenStreetMap land cover (ODbL) with its Davenport z0, in the footprints' frame — wire them into City Surface's Layer Outlines, Layer Names, Layer Roughness and Flatten.

